From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:46:24 +0900
Subject: Hooks for a backend nested in a host that differs from a desktop
 compositor

What src/backends/android (the last patch) needs from upstream code, as virtual functions
whose base versions keep upstream behaviour, so the Android host's specifics stay in one place
and upstream changes meet them at these hooks only (docs/72):

- WaylandOutput: hostScale(), ownsScale(), singleSurface() (a host that shows the output's
  buffer pixel for pixel, lets KWin choose the scale, and presents the primary layer on the
  output surface itself), mapFromHost() for input positions, modesFor(), applyExtraChanges(),
  hasCursorLayer(), and an optional host wl_output to be fullscreen on.
- WaylandBackend: createOutputObject(), configureDisplay(), renderDevicePath(),
  setUpRenderDevice(), createShmAllocator(), implicitSync(), hostImportsClientBuffers(),
  hostFingerScrollIsNatural(); createOutput(), addOutput(), removeOutput() for derived
  backends' outputs.
- WaylandDisplay: a connect timeout, a connection-lost handler, and globalAnnounced()/
  globalRemoved() so a derived backend binds globals of its own.
- DrmDevice::setAllocator(); ShmGraphicsBufferAllocator in a directory instead of memfds;
  EglDisplay::create() with the render node; OutputBackend::maxLinuxDmabufVersion(), used when
  the server creates zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1; InputRedirection::idleInhibitedChanged().

Replaces the environment-variable checks (MOTO_KWIN_FLAT_OUTPUT, MOTO_KWIN_RENDER_DEVICE,
MOTO_GPU_ALLOCATOR, MOTO_KWIN_ANDROID_SHM) that the earlier patches spread over these files.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [hooks for the Android host backend; upstream behaviour unchanged when not overridden]
X-Rungic-Tests: L1:full KWin test suite equals the unpatched baseline (host, docs/72); L3:session.ready L3:display.geometry L3:perf.compositor
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/72
Origin: vendor
